\par Adult ogres stand 9 to 10 feet tall and weigh 600 to 650 pounds. Their skin color ranges from dull yellow to dull brown. Their clothing consists of poorly cured furs and hides, which add to their naturally repellent odor.
\par Ogres speak Giant, and those specimens who boast Intelligence scores of at least 10 also speak Common.
\par }{COMBAT
\par }{\fs20 Ogres favor overwhelming odds, sneak attacks, and ambushes over a fair fight. They are intelligent enough to fire ranged weapons first to soften up their foes before closing, but ogre gangs and bands fight as unorganized individuals.
\par }{\fs20\cf0 
\par }\pard\plain \s16\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\loch\af28\hich\af28\dbch\af28\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0 OGRE BARBARIAN
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\cf1\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20\cf0 Their inherent bent toward chaos combines with their size and}{\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 
strength to make ogres natural barbarians. Indeed, their leaders}{\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 are almost always barbarians of low to middle level, monstrous}{\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 brutes whose fury in battle is truly fearsome. A raging ogre barbarian}{
\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 is an inspiration to other ogres.
\par }\pard\plain \s16\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\loch\af28\hich\af28\dbch\af28\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0 COMBAT}{\fs20\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\cf1\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20\cf0 Marginally more intelligent than his brutish fellows, an ogre barbarian}{\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 
is slightly more likely to enter a fair fight, but in general}{\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 prefers the brutish tactics common to all its kind.
\par }{\b\fs20\cf0 Rage (Ex): }{\fs20\cf0 Twice per day, an ogre barbarian can enter a state of}{\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 fierce rage that last for 9 rounds. The following changes are in}{\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 
effect as long as he rages: AC 17 (touch 8, flat-footed 17); hp 95;}{\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 Atk +18/+13 melee (2d6+16, }{\i\fs20\cf0 +1 greatclub}{\fs20\cf0 ); SV Fort +14, Will +4; Str}{\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 
30, Con 22; Climb +15, Jump +16. At the end of his rage, the ogre}{\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 barbarian is fatigued for the duration}{\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 of the encounter.
\par }{\b\fs20\cf0 Trap Sense (Ex):}{\fs20\cf0  An ogre barbarian}{\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 has a +1 bonus on Reflex}{\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 saves made to avoid traps. He}{\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 also has a +1 bonus to his AC}{\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 
against attacks by traps.
\par }{\b\fs20\cf0 Uncanny Dodge (Ex):}{\b\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 An ogre barbarian retains}{\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 his Dex bonus to AC regardless}{\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 of being caught}{\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 flat-footed or attacked}{\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 
by an invisible}{\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 opponent. His}{\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 Dex bonus to AC is}{\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 +0, but this means that}{\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 he is not subject to a}{\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 rogue\rquote s sneak attack in}{
\fs20\cf0  }{\fs20\cf0 these circumstances.}{\fs20\cf0 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20\cf0 
\par }{MERROW
\par }{\fs20 These cousins of the ogre have the aquatic subtype.
\par They dwell in freshwater lakes and rivers. They have a base land speed of 30 feet and a swim speed of 40 feet and are found only in aquatic environments.
\par Instead of the typical ogre\rquote s greatclub, they prefer to use longspears in melee (attack +8 melee, damage 1d8+7).
\par }{OGRES AS CHARACTERS
\par }{\fs20 Ogre characters possess the following racial traits.
\par \emdash  +10 Strength, \endash 2 Dexterity, +4 Constitution, \endash 4 Intelligence, \endash 4 Charisma.
\par \emdash Large size. \endash 1 penalty to Armor Class, \endash 1 penalty on attack rolls, \endash 4 penalty on Hide checks, +4 bonus on grapple checks, lifting and carrying limits double those of Medium characters.
\par \emdash Space/Reach: 10 feet/10 feet.
\par \emdash An ogre\rquote s base land speed is 40 feet.
\par \emdash Darkvision out to 60 feet.
\par \emdash Racial Hit Dice: An ogre begins with four levels of giant, which provide 4d8 Hit Dice, a base attack bonus of +3, and base saving throw bonuses of Fort +4, Ref +1, and Will +1. 
\par \emdash Racial Skills: An ogre\rquote s giant levels give it skill points equal to 7 x (2 + Int modifier, minimum 1). Its class skills are Climb, Listen, and Spot.
\par \emdash Racial Feats: An ogre\rquote s giant levels give it two feats.
\par \emdash Weapon and Armor Proficiency: An ogre is automatically proficient with simple weapons, martial weapons, light and medium armor, and shields.
\par \emdash  +5 natural armor bonus.
\par \emdash Automatic Languages: Common, Giant. Bonus Languages: Dwarven, Orc, Goblin, Terran.
\par \emdash Favored Class: Barbarian.
\par \emdash Level adjustment +2.
\par }
\pard 
\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 The body of a mature purple worm is 5 feet in diameter and 80 feet long, weighing about 40,000 pounds. The creature has a poisonous stinger in its tail.
\par }{COMBAT
\par }{\fs20 In battle, a purple worm forms into a coil 20 feet in diameter, biting and stinging anything within reach.
\par }{\b\fs20 Improved Grab (Ex): }{\fs20 To use this ability, a purple worm must hit with its bite attack. It can then attempt to start a grapple as a free action without provoking an attack of opportunity. If it wins the grapple che
ck, it establishes a hold and can attempt to swallow the foe the following round.
\par }{\b\fs20 Poison (Ex): }{\fs20 Injury, Fortitude DC 25, initial damage 1d6 Str, secondary damage 2d6 Str. The save DC is Constitution-based.
\par }{\b\fs20 Swallow Whole (Ex):}{\fs20  A purple worm can try to swallo
w a grabbed opponent of a smaller size than itself by making a successful grapple check. Once inside, the opponent takes 2d8+12 points of crushing damage plus 8 points of acid damage per round from the worm\rquote 
s gizzard. A swallowed creature can cut its way o
ut by using a light slashing or piercing weapon to deal 25 points of damage to the gizzard (AC 17). Once the creature exits, muscular action closes the hole; another swallowed opponent must cut its own way out. A Gargantuan worm\rquote 
s interior can hold 2 Large, 8 Medium, 32 Small, 128 Tiny, or 512 Diminutive or smaller opponents.
\par }{\b\fs20 Skills:}{\fs20  A purple worm has a +8 racial bonus on any Swim check to perform some special action or avoid a hazard. It can always choose to take 10 on a Swim check, even if distracted or e
ndangered. It can use the run action while swimming, provided it swims in a straight line.
\par }{\fs36 
